{"shortDescription":"BUENOS AIRES, Argentina, Sept. 8, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- Cresud S.A.C.I.F. y A. (NASDAQ:CRESY, BYMA: CRES), leading Argentine agricultural company, announces today its results for FY 2026 ended June 30, 2026.HIGHLIGHTSThe Company's market capitalization as of June 30, 2026, was approximately USD 795…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["BUENOS AIRES, Argentina, Sept. 8, 2026 /PRNewswire/ -- ",{"type":"b","children":["Cresud S.A.C.I.F. y A. (",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"NASDAQ:CRESY","text":"NASDAQ:CRESY"}},", BYMA: CRES), leading Argentine agricultural company, announces today its results for FY 2026 ended June 30, 2026."]}]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["HIGHLIGHTS"]}]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":["Net income for fiscal year 2026 amounted to ARS 372,280 million, compared to a gain of ARS 299,635 million in the previous fiscal year."]},{"type":"*","children":["Adjusted EBITDA from agribusiness segments reached ARS 17,812 million, while the Urban Properties and Investments segment (through IRSA) recorded ARS 291,055 million."]},{"type":"*","children":["The 2026 campaign was carried out with a larger planted area across the region, amid rising commodity prices and input costs and highly favorable weather conditions, except in certain production regions, mainly in Brazil. We planted 314,000 hectares, approximately 5% more than in the previous campaign, and achieved record grain production, exceeding one million tons."]},{"type":"*","children":["Argentina recorded excellent production results, with record wheat production and strong soybean and corn yields. BrasilAgro faced a more challenging campaign, particularly in sugarcane due to weather conditions, fires and operational issues, while other crops performed in line with expectations, although with tighter margins."]},{"type":"*","children":["Livestock activity reached record levels of cattle production, prices and margins, supported by continued production intensification through feedlots and investments in infrastructure."]},{"type":"*","children":["In agricultural real estate, during the fiscal year BrasilAgro agreed to sell a 921-hectare portion of the Morotí farm in Paraguay for USD 1.5 million, of which 372 hectares, representing approximately USD 0.6 million, were recognized as of fiscal year-end."]},{"type":"*","children":["On the financial front, during the fiscal year we issued approximately USD 256 million in notes, reducing the Company's average financing cost and extending maturity. In addition, the warrant program issued in 2021 was completed, and we distributed ARS 93,800 million in dividends, representing an approximate 8% dividend yield."]}]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":3,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Financial Highlights"]},"(In millions of Argentine Pesos)FY 2026 ended June 30, 2026"]}]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"hidden":true}},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"hidden":true}}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Income Statement"]}]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["06/30/2026"]}]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["06/30/2025"]}]}]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":["Agricultural Business Revenue"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"children":[{"type":"p","children":["727,486"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","params":{"colspan":1,"rowspan":1},"child